{"name":"Nantucket Mist","hex":"#cabfbf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nantucket","blocks":[{"text":"Nantucket is an island in Massachusetts, United States, about 30 miles (48 km) south of the Cape Cod peninsula. Together with the small islands of Tuckernuck and Muskeget, it constitutes the Town and County of Nantucket, a combined county/town government. Nantucket is the southeasternmost town in Massachusetts. The name \"Nantucket\" is adapted from similar Algonquian names for the island."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Nantucket-08-2004.jpg/330px-Nantucket-08-2004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nantucket","wikidata":"Q49149"},{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mist","wikidata":"Q192196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Clinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg/500px-Clinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Clinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg/500px-Clinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clinton Folger, mail carrier for Nantucket, towed his car to the state highway for driving to Siasconset, in observance of an early 20th-century ban on automobiles on town roads.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/48/Hsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg/500px-Hsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/48/Hsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg/500px-Hsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1870s street scene on Nantucket","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg/500px-The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg/1280px-The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 